Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 17:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 70/70] Set gecko-camera chroma subsampling

The gecko-camera decoder supplies YUV 4:2:0 frames: the luma plane is full
size and the chroma planes are half width and half height.  ESR115 defaults
VideoData::YCbCrBuffer to full chroma sampling, which makes
CreateAndCopyData() read the chroma planes as if they matched the luma
dimensions.

Set the actual sampling mode before handing the frame to Gecko.  This avoids
reading past the mapped chroma buffers while copying decoded video frames.
---
 dom/media/platforms/gecko-camera/GeckoCameraVideoDecoder.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/dom/media/platforms/gecko-camera/GeckoCameraVideoDecoder.cpp b/dom/media/platforms/gecko-camera/GeckoCameraVideoDecoder.cpp
index 4cf5b6476935..2d19e422f8b7 100644
--- a/dom/media/platforms/gecko-camera/GeckoCameraVideoDecoder.cpp
+++ b/dom/media/platforms/gecko-camera/GeckoCameraVideoDecoder.cpp
@@ -192,6 +192,7 @@ void GeckoCameraVideoDecoder::onDecodedYCbCrFrame(const gecko::camera::YCbCrFram
   buffer.mYUVColorSpace = DefaultColorSpace({frame->width, frame->height});
   buffer.mColorDepth = gfx::ColorDepth::COLOR_8;
   buffer.mColorRange = gfx::ColorRange::LIMITED;
+  buffer.mChromaSubsampling = gfx::ChromaSubsampling::HALF_WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT;
 
   gfx::IntRect pictureRegion(0, 0, frame->width, frame->height);
   RefPtr<MediaData> data = VideoData::CreateAndCopyData(
